      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Founded in 1971, the Grass Lake Area Historical Society preserves local history and operates the Coe House Museum, a 1870s home turned exhibit space.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5,
        8,
        18,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://glahs.org/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Coe House Museum opened in 1972 after the society purchased Myrta Coe’s former home, transforming it into a public museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://glahs.org/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A self‑guided historic walking tour loops through downtown Grass Lake, highlighting landmarks and stories that bring the village’s past to life.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grasslakedowntownmi.gov/historic/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1971 Grass Lake celebrated its centennial, prompting the community to dedicate a historic home as a museum to honor its heritage.",
